{"ts":"2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"96b2f4f37551cb3935f93353","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-o8z748"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-896: heterogeneous atomic specification batches need batch-local references and one discoverable SDK-first CLI path"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue #896 shows that plan materialize applies one shared type and field set to every child. The existing pm item mutate surface already provides heterogeneous atomic create/update/close rows, dry-run, compensation, and resume, but the reported workflow cannot discover it and explicit stable ids prevent an epic plus forward-referencing children from being authored as one coherent specification document."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:cli","area:sdk","atomic","context-management","github-report","structured-input","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":480},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Public SDK exposes a typed resolver for heterogeneous atomic mutation documents with unique batch-local aliases, stable explicit-or-derived ids, and forward references in parent/dependency fields; pm item mutate accepts the versioned document through its existing stdin path, validates and previews the fully resolved batch before writes, and returns alias-to-id outcomes without adding a competing top-level batch command; CLI, MCP, contracts, completion, SDK docs, errors, token budgets, and 100 percent coverage stay aligned; malformed aliases, cycles, duplicates, unknown references, and replay mismatches fail before tracker mutation; An isolated npm and Bun consumer authors and reads back a mixed Epic/Feature/Decision graph atomically, and a forced mid-batch failure proves compensation leaves no partial active specification"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make one coherent heterogeneous specification authorable as one atomic SDK-owned mutation document"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Agents preserve peak authoring context, avoid orphaned children, and pay one bootstrap instead of one process per item"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Turns the existing atomic mutation substrate into a discoverable universal project-creation primitive without adding a competing command grammar"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"One dry-runnable batch can create mixed item types with per-row metadata and forward references, returning a stable alias-to-id receipt"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The shipped primitive exists but real users still conclude batching is impossible; the remaining composition and discovery gap is now evidenced by GH-896"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"pm CLI 2026.8.4, Node 22/24/26, Linux/macOS/Windows; CLI, public SDK, MCP, completions, contracts, packed npm and Bun consumers"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Create one Plan with multiple steps; pm plan materialize accepts only one materialize type/tags/field set. pm item mutate accepts heterogeneous rows but requires every stable id up front and documents no batch-local forward-reference vocabulary."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A single atomic document creates an Epic, Features, Decisions, and their dependencies with per-row metadata and batch-local aliases; dry-run validates the resolved graph without writes."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Plan materialization is shape-uniform, while the atomic mutation surface requires preallocated ids and is not discoverable from create/plan workflows."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"Agents spend one tool call per item, manually correlate ids, and can leave partially authored specifications when a later create fails."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-4e12","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-cyn0y6","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-j82fd3","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-usfg","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-xm7c","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-y9hq","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"text=Duplicate check 2026-08-05: searched all statuses for the exact GH-896 title and for batch item creation, plan materialize, heterogeneous create, commitWorkspaceTransaction, commitItemMutations, structured mutation, atomic create, and forward references. Closed pm-y9hq owns the SDK transaction primitive and closed pm-xm7c owns the existing CLI/MCP JSON batch; neither provides batch-local references or fixes discovery from create/plan. GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/896"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"b0b37132babd70389a960bcd4e4ac6579914ba5fb9ed1df3014234e5263bcdd1","message":""}
